sxml decode - Write an EXI stream as an XML document

Usage: sxml decode [--alignment=ALIGNMENT] [--preserve=LIST] [--fragment] [--strict] [--self-contained] [--block-size=N] [--value-max-length=N] [--value-partition-capacity=N] [--schema=FILE] [--output=FILE] [--force] INPUT

Reads INPUT as an EXI 1.0 stream (Efficient XML Interchange) and
writes the document to standard output as XML text, by the xml
method with its default parameters.

A stream whose header carries its options is read with them. One
that does not is read with the options its encoder was given, which
the flags repeat: --alignment, --preserve, --fragment, --strict,
--block-size, --value-max-length and --value-partition-capacity, as
for sxml encode. --schema=FILE reads it with the schema-informed
grammars of the XSD in FILE. Without --preserve=prefixes the decoder
makes the prefixes up (ns0, ns1, ...).

--output=FILE (-o FILE) writes the document to FILE instead, and only
when the command succeeds; a FILE that exists is replaced only with
--force.

A stream that is not EXI, or not well-formed EXI, is reported on
standard error as
  INPUT: byte N: message

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 when INPUT is not an EXI stream sxml can
read, 2 for a bad option value, 3 when a file cannot be read or
written.

Options:
  -h, --help                        Show this help and exit
      --alignment=ALIGNMENT         EXI alignment of the stream (one of: bit-packed, byte-alignment, pre-compression, compression; default: bit-packed)
      --preserve=LIST               EXI fidelity: comments,pis,dtd,prefixes,lexical-values
      --fragment                    The EXI stream is a fragment, not a document
      --strict                      Strict schema-informed EXI grammars
      --self-contained              The EXI stream may hold self-contained elements
      --block-size=N                EXI values per compression block
      --value-max-length=N          Longest EXI value kept in the string table
      --value-partition-capacity=N  Most EXI values in the string table
      --schema=FILE                 XSD of the stream's schema-informed grammars
  -o, --output=FILE                 Write the result to FILE instead of standard output
      --force                       Replace files that exist instead of refusing

Arguments:
  INPUT  EXI stream to decode; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml decode orders.exi
  sxml decode --alignment=compression --output=orders.xml orders.exi
